{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0117rDaWbp8nsX9WCj2dSt8t","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"The RPC names were not renamed: they remained **AddTopicsToMirror** and **RemoveTopicsFromMirror** throughout the KIP-1279 Cluster Mirroring design discussion, with only the method signatures changing.\\\\n\\\\nSupporting facts in time order:\\\\n\\\\n- 2026-03-13T17:03:08Z - Federico Valeri confirms the signature change: \\\\\\\"All topic-scoped mirror RPCs now consistently follow the (String mirrorName, Set<String> topics) pattern,\\\\\\\" i.e. Admin.addTopicsToMirror(String mirrorName, Set<String> topics, AddTopicsToMirrorOptions options) and Admin.removeTopicsFromMirror(String mirrorName, Set<String> topics, RemoveTopicsFromMirrorOptions options) - the names themselves were retained, not renamed [mail:cdc51b19d028bc0f5c373cf1].\\\\n\\\\nWhat could not be determined: The question presupposes a rename to different names, but no such rename appears in the examined records; the names AddTopicsToMirror/RemoveTopicsFromMirror (and their camelCase forms) were used consistently from the start of the discussion through the final signature confirmation. No alternative final names were found.\\\\n\\\\nCould not be determined from the records: the values 2026-02-18T17:33:31Z, 2026-02-20T19:39:32Z, 2026-03-06T13:41:52Z, 2026-03-08T20:58:07Z, 2026-03-10T20:19:50Z, 2026-03-13T12:56:54Z, and asks whether it is missing the mirrorName (removed: not found in the retrieved records).\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"mail:cdc51b19d028bc0f5c373cf1\\\",\\\"mail:44843036d638b29f0550d70c\\\",\\\"mail:0a9bb7f24cac428cae178e83\\\",\\\"mail:3ff994af98687f284b08fecb\\\",\\\"mail:b32b985603ecf53569b819c6\\\",\\\"mail:5d73dbf07c94c92bd8490ec2\\\",\\\"mail:9fe071745db2786e61f33354\\\",\\\"mail:ed059e838b132d6e650a0e3d\\\",\\\"mail:4474ff38b1b9930dc245e316\\\",\\\"mail:5a9e0efe4aaeb97679a07aca\\\",\\\"mail:ec6ea0cd50ab7f257f